From: Jose Ignacio Tornos Martinez <jtornosm@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: add device-specific reset for Qualcomm SDX62/SDX65 modems

Backport of the modem half of the pending upstream series "PCI: Add
device-specific reset for Qualcomm devices" (v12, linux-pci, June 2026).

The RG520N-EB on this board enumerates as the plain Qualcomm 17cb:0308 and
implements no FLR, while its root port has no usable secondary bus reset
(reset_subordinate returns -ENOTTY). pci_reset_supported() is therefore false:
/sys/bus/pci/devices/.../reset does not even exist, and the MHI driver's
recovery path dies at pci_try_reset_function() with -25 -- HW-observed here,
leaving the modem unreachable until the board is rebooted.

The SDX6x does have a hardware reset: the MHI SoC reset request register at
BAR0 + 0xb0. Register it as a device-specific reset so pci_try_reset_function()
has something to call. mhi-pci-generic already implements .reset_prepare and
.reset_done, so the reset also works with the driver bound -- including from
userspace, which makes it testable on a healthy modem instead of only during a
failure.

Deviation from upstream: only the modem entry is taken. The series also adds
reset_qualcomm_wlan() for WCN6855 (17cb:1103) and WCN7850 (17cb:1107); this
board's companion radio is a QCN9074 (17cb:1104), which is not covered by
either, and that function carries review comments of its own.

Upstream status at backport time: v12 reviewed, v13 planned, not yet merged.
Drop this patch once it lands.

Signed-off-by: Muhammad Huda Nugroho <mhudan21@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -4236,6 +4236,45 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+#define MHI_SOC_RESET_REQ_OFFSET		0xb0
+#define MHI_SOC_RESET_REQ			BIT(0)
+
+/*
+ * Qualcomm modem device-specific reset using MHI SoC reset via BAR0
+ * register.
+ */
+static int reset_qualcomm_modem(struct pci_dev *pdev, bool probe)
+{
+	void __iomem *bar;
+	u16 cmd;
+
+	if (probe)
+		return 0;
+
+	if (pdev->current_state != PCI_D0)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	pci_read_config_word(pdev, PCI_COMMAND, &cmd);
+	pci_write_config_word(pdev, PCI_COMMAND, cmd | PCI_COMMAND_MEMORY);
+
+	bar = pci_iomap(pdev, 0, 0);
+	if (!bar) {
+		pci_write_config_word(pdev, PCI_COMMAND, cmd);
+		return -ENODEV;
+	}
+
+	iowrite32(MHI_SOC_RESET_REQ, bar + MHI_SOC_RESET_REQ_OFFSET);
+	ioread32(bar + MHI_SOC_RESET_REQ_OFFSET);
+
+	/* Be sure device reset has been executed */
+	msleep(2000);
+
+	pci_iounmap(pdev, bar);
+	pci_write_config_word(pdev, PCI_COMMAND, cmd);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static const struct pci_dev_reset_methods pci_dev_reset_methods[] = {
 	{ PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL, PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_82599_SFP_VF,
 		 reset_intel_82599_sfp_virtfn },
@@ -4251,6 +4290,7 @@
 		reset_chelsio_generic_dev },
 	{ PCI_VENDOR_ID_HUAWEI, PCI_DEVICE_ID_HINIC_VF,
 		reset_hinic_vf_dev },
+	{ PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x0308, reset_qualcomm_modem }, /* SDX62/SDX65 modems */
 	{ 0 }
 };
 
